# Go
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Build artifact and database from the README's own instructions
/portico
# And the copies of it that get set aside before a rebuild — rebuilding over
# a binary that is currently running breaks its signature on macOS, so the
# working answer is to move it out of the way first. Ignored because the one
# that appeared was 40MB, untracked, and therefore listed in `git status`
# alongside real work: exactly the thing a hurried `git add -A` sweeps into
# the history.
/portico.bak.*
# `go build ./...` writes every main package's binary to the working
# directory, so the example lands here too — nobody asked for it and it is
# 40MB.
/mock-sp
# The example's SAML key, certificate, and metadata document. The key has to
# survive a restart — Portico encrypts assertions to whatever key the
# registered metadata published — so it is written to disk, and a private
# key in a repository is a private key in a repository even when it is a
# demonstration's.
/.mock-sp/
/portico.db
/portico.db-shm
/portico.db-wal
# The name this project had before it was Portico. A local database from
# that era was committed once; the pattern stays so it cannot happen again.
/keylite.db
/keylite.db-shm
/keylite.db-wal

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Working notes for a long task, kept out of the repository. They accumulate
# the things a scratch file accumulates — the demo tenant's password, which
# database was dropped, what a history rewrite removed — none of which
# belongs in a published identity product, and all of which someone will
# copy because it is written down next to instructions that work.
/TASK_CONTEXT_*.md

# A pull request description, written to a file so it can be handed to
# `gh pr create --body-file`. It describes one branch at one moment, so
# committing it leaves a permanent file that is wrong the day after it
# merges. It was committed once, by a `git add -A` that picked it up while
# it was untracked, and was out of date within the hour.
/PR_DESCRIPTION.md

# Frontend
web/node_modules/

# Browser test output: traces, screenshots, and the HTML report. Kept as a
# CI artifact on failure, never committed.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/blob-report/
web/.playwright/

# Built frontend: the directory must exist for go:embed, but its contents
# are build output. See internal/web/embed.go.
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/.gitkeep

# GoReleaser output
/dist/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Documentation built into the binary; see hack/build-docs.sh
internal/docs/site/*
!internal/docs/site/.gitkeep
